ose graph is shown. The function f is defined by f(x) = k(x)/g(x), using this original quotient. What is the domain of f?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"All real numbers"},{"key":"B","text":"All real numbers except −1 and 2"},{"key":"C","text":"All real numbers except −1, 1 and 3"},{"key":"D","text":"All real numbers except −2, 1 and 3"},{"key":"E","text":"The domain cannot be determined"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"D. The numerator is defined for all real x. The original quotient is undefined where g(x) = 0, namely x = −2, 1 and 3. Those values remain excluded even if a common factor could later be canceled. Every other real value is allowed.","assets":{"source":"Eng Abdelrahman Ghoneem — reviewed instructor adaptation","source_question_id":"GH-REVIEW-20261005-rational-domain","source_ids_adapted":["30eec906-1afb-5d4e-afd6-a9f868417e15"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Clarify an ambiguous source item in an explicitly authored adaptation.","curriculum_lesson":"Functions and transformations","lesson_subtopic":"Domain of a rational function","lesson_taxonomy_version":"20260929","verified_release":"20261005-reviewed-exam-versions","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 300\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Graph of (x+2)(x-1)(x-3)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"420\" height=\"300\" fill=\"white\"/><line x1=\"48.00\" y1=\"142.50\" x2=\"394.00\" y2=\"142.50\" stroke=\"#708196\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"197.62\" y1=\"260.00\" x2=\"197.62\" y2=\"25.00\" stroke=\"#708196\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"57.35\" y1=\"138.50\" x2=\"57.35\" y2=\"146.50\" stroke=\"#708196\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"57.35\" y=\"162.50\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#15263d\">-3</text><line x1=\"104.11\" y1=\"138.50\" x2=\"104.11\" y2=\"146.50\" stroke=\"#708196\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"104.11\" y=\"162.50\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle